cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use jaxnu in your research, please cite the software itself (below)
  and, once available, the accompanying paper (see "preferred-citation").
type: software
title: "jaxnu: an autodiff-first neutrino oscillation engine in JAX"
version: 0.2.3
date-released: "2026-07-28"
authors:
  - family-names: Granger
    given-names: Pierre
    affiliation: "CERN"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8333-4393"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pgranger23/jaxnu-osc"
url: "https://github.com/pgranger23/jaxnu-osc"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - neutrino oscillations
  - automatic differentiation
  - JAX
  - matter effects
  - PREM
  - non-standard interactions
  - sterile neutrinos
abstract: >-
  jaxnu is a neutrino oscillation calculator written in JAX, differentiable
  end-to-end with respect to both the oscillation parameters and the
  propagation geometry. It supports vacuum, constant-density matter, the
  layered PREM Earth (with atmospheric production height), arbitrary
  user-supplied density profiles, and adiabatic solar propagation, with
  non-standard interactions and 3+N sterile neutrinos as first-class
  extensions.
